WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.056 --> 00:00:19.158
Patrick thought, staring in dismay at Mickey's catcher's mitt.

2
00:00:19.898 --> 00:00:23.801
Daniel had just told Patrick that Coach rarely started seventh-graders like Patrick.

3
00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:29.284
This kid—an eighth-grader—would probably bump Patrick down to a backup catcher.

4
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.501
"There goes my fantastic baseball season," thought Patrick gloomily.

5
00:00:35.421 --> 00:00:39.703
Just then Coach approached the dugout, his gray hair tucked under a Dragons cap.

6
00:00:43.284 --> 00:00:45.144
"I see you two have met," he said.

7
00:00:45.164 --> 00:00:48.345
"Daniel's gonna coach the pitchers and catchers this year.

8
00:00:49.485 --> 00:00:51.446
I just informed him that he's got a new player.

9
00:00:52.266 --> 00:00:54.587
We're glad you moved here, Mickey," Coach added.

10
00:00:54.607 --> 00:00:57.047
"We need a good relief catcher."

11
00:00:58.668 --> 00:01:00.224
"Phew!" Patrick thought.

12
00:01:00.765 --> 00:01:02.806
Coach had just called Mickey a "relief" catcher.

13
00:01:03.346 --> 00:01:05.728
That had to mean that Coach thought of Patrick as starter.

14
00:01:06.608 --> 00:01:08.289
Coach jerked a thumb toward the field.

15
00:01:08.309 --> 00:01:09.990
"Get out there, you two.

16
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.652
Daniel's waiting for you."

17
00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.013
After warm-ups, practice went into full swing.

18
00:01:15.733 --> 00:01:17.174
Patrick crouched behind the plate.

19
00:01:18.255 --> 00:01:21.777
Dell threw pitch after pitch as Daniel stood right behind Patrick.

20
00:01:22.717 --> 00:01:24.178
"Not fast enough, Patrick!"

21
00:01:24.599 --> 00:01:25.279
yelled Daniel.

22
00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:26.760
"Too stiff!"

23
00:01:27.996 --> 00:01:29.477
"Stand higher on your toes!"

24
00:01:30.237 --> 00:01:32.939
Patrick felt stung by his brother's constant criticism.

25
00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.080
"What is his problem?"

26
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:35.800
he thought.

27
00:01:36.761 --> 00:01:40.683
Mickey returned from his turn in the batting cage and came over to watch Patrick and Dell.

28
00:01:42.224 --> 00:01:44.865
Dell threw a fastball on the outside edge of the plate.

29
00:01:46.066 --> 00:01:47.607
Patrick reached for it but missed.

30
00:01:47.627 --> 00:01:51.489
"You should have had that one!"

31
00:01:51.869 --> 00:01:52.569
yelled Daniel.

32
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.252
Patrick glared at him, even more embarrassed now that Mickey was watching.

33
00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:02.341
He threw the ball back to Dell and then glanced at the bleachers, where his father sat watching

34
00:02:02.381 --> 00:02:07.323
practice. Dad shrugged, signaling to Patrick that everybody misses sometimes.

35
00:02:07.343 --> 00:02:10.704
"Patrick! Keep your head in the game!"

36
00:02:11.124 --> 00:02:11.884
Daniel snapped.

37
00:02:12.844 --> 00:02:14.785
"Eyes on the field, not the bleachers!"

38
00:02:14.805 --> 00:02:17.666
"Got it," muttered Patrick.

39
00:02:18.506 --> 00:02:21.527
Finally Coach called Patrick and Dell over to the batting cage.

40
00:02:22.387 --> 00:02:26.148
Mickey and Jerry, a relief pitcher, moved to home plate to work with Daniel.

41
00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.742
Dell went into the batting cage first.

42
00:02:34.365 --> 00:02:37.868
Patrick wanted to watch Mickey catch, to assess the other catcher's skills.

43
00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:42.252
But he forced himself to pay attention to Coach's batting instructions instead.

44
00:02:43.513 --> 00:02:48.097
Patrick was too light to have a power swing, so he needed to master the mechanics of batting.

45
00:02:48.878 --> 00:02:50.499
Coach guided Dell into position.

46
00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.404
"It's one hundred percent physics, plus ten percent attitude," he said.

47
00:02:56.332 --> 00:02:59.634
Patrick and a few other players groaned at Coach's lame joke.

48
00:03:00.494 --> 00:03:02.015
Todd stepped closer to Patrick.

49
00:03:02.035 --> 00:03:05.577
"Did you see that new kid hit?"

50
00:03:06.618 --> 00:03:09.359
"Nope." Patrick shook his head, keeping his eyes on Dell.

51
00:03:09.379 --> 00:03:10.960
"Is he any good?"

52
00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:16.363
"Unbelievable! He whacked that ball like he was shooting for the moon.

53
00:03:17.183 --> 00:03:18.764
He'll be a pinch hitter for sure."

54
00:03:18.784 --> 00:03:25.148
"We'll need a new pinch hitter if you start in left field, Todd," said Buck, their first baseman.

55
00:03:26.176 --> 00:03:26.837
Todd nodded.

56
00:03:26.857 --> 00:03:29.259
"Mickey could definitely get the job."

57
00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.721
Patrick groaned inwardly.

58
00:03:32.441 --> 00:03:35.344
In baseball a pinch hitter came in to hit for another batter.

59
00:03:36.225 --> 00:03:38.767
The player he replaced was out for the rest of the game.

60
00:03:39.407 --> 00:03:44.031
So if Mickey was called in to pinch hit for somebody, Mickey would replace Patrick as catcher.

61
00:03:44.872 --> 00:03:47.774
A few minutes later, it was Patrick's turn in the batting cage.

62
00:03:48.735 --> 00:03:51.557
He set his feet, relaxed into position, and nodded.

63
00:03:52.278 --> 00:03:54.420
He was ready for the machine to release a pitch.

64
00:03:55.592 --> 00:03:59.815
Swoosh! The ball sailed past Patrick and slammed into the net.

65
00:04:01.656 --> 00:04:02.556
"We'll try another one.

66
00:04:02.716 --> 00:04:10.240
But first Coach came over to adjust Patrick's forward arm and then stepped back.

67
00:04:11.441 --> 00:04:14.483
Ping! This time Patrick tipped the ball.

68
00:04:15.363 --> 00:04:18.505
Whack! The next time he had a solid hit.

69
00:04:18.845 --> 00:04:19.966
It was at least a single.

70
00:04:21.487 --> 00:04:23.608
Coach watched Patrick hit a few more times.

71
00:04:25.216 --> 00:04:26.117
"Not bad, Patrick.

72
00:04:26.477 --> 00:04:27.278
You're meeting the ball.

73
00:04:27.998 --> 00:04:30.100
Spend some time on the weights, building up your strength.

74
00:04:31.241 --> 00:04:32.842
We need to get a few doubles out of you.

75
00:04:33.382 --> 00:04:33.902
Next up!"

76
00:04:35.043 --> 00:04:39.106
Patrick left the cage and glanced at home plate, where Daniel was still working with Mickey.

77
00:04:40.027 --> 00:04:41.808
Patrick tried to read Daniel's expression.

78
00:04:42.509 --> 00:04:47.592
Daniel looked "Impressed," thought Patrick.

79
00:04:47.612 --> 00:04:50.675
"You've got good speed and good instincts, Mickey," Daniel said.

80
00:04:50.695 --> 00:04:52.396
"And you know how to use them."

81
00:04:53.644 --> 00:04:55.526
Dell was also watching Daniel and Mickey.

82
00:04:56.146 --> 00:04:58.508
"Don't sweat it, Patrick," he said quietly.

83
00:04:58.528 --> 00:05:04.312
"Mickey's good, but he's new, and he's gonna need time to get used to working with our team.

84
00:05:05.293 --> 00:05:07.755
I think Coach will start you—he's seen you play.

85
00:05:08.415 --> 00:05:09.896
Plus, you're Daniel's brother."

86
00:05:10.657 --> 00:05:12.898
Patrick nodded, but his throat felt tight.

87
00:05:13.539 --> 00:05:17.382
He was worried about Mickey, and he didn't like being linked to Daniel all the time.

88
00:05:17.402 --> 00:05:20.244
"We'll see," he said with a shrug.

89
00:05:21.332 --> 00:05:24.193
An hour later parents started arriving to pick up their kids.

90
00:05:25.074 --> 00:05:27.795
Coach called the team into the dugout before ending practice.

91
00:05:27.815 --> 00:05:29.936
"Good start, boys."

92
00:05:30.476 --> 00:05:33.317
He looked down the line of players, meeting each of their eyes.

93
00:05:33.337 --> 00:05:36.038
"How many of you have homework this weekend?"

94
00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:37.919
Everyone raised a hand.

95
00:05:37.939 --> 00:05:39.740
"Get it done.

96
00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:43.422
Having baseball practice is no excuse for slacking on grades.

97
00:05:44.242 --> 00:05:45.502
See you on Monday after school."

98
00:05:46.623 --> 00:05:48.964
Patrick walked out of the dugout with Dell and Daniel.

99
00:05:51.872 --> 00:05:54.154
Mr. Deboe climbed down from the bleachers to join them.

100
00:05:54.174 --> 00:05:58.578
"What did you think of the new kid, Dad?"

101
00:05:58.918 --> 00:05:59.599
Daniel asked.

102
00:05:59.619 --> 00:06:03.262
"He looks confident behind the plate," said Mr.

103
00:06:03.282 --> 00:06:05.905
Deboe. "Yeah," agreed Daniel.

104
00:06:05.925 --> 00:06:07.726
"He's got sharp instincts."

105
00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:09.928
"Good," said Mr.

106
00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:13.411
Deboe. Patrick trailed behind them into the parking lot.

107
00:06:13.431 --> 00:06:17.535
"What about me?"

108
00:06:17.855 --> 00:06:18.256
he thought.

109
00:06:19.224 --> 00:06:23.787
Weren't his dad and brother concerned that Patrick would probably lose his position as starter?

110
00:06:26.288 --> 00:06:28.629
Just then a horn beeped, and Patrick looked up.

111
00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:33.032
An old van painted to look like a giant dog sat in the parking lot.

112
00:06:33.892 --> 00:06:37.915
It had eyes and ears sticking up on top and a tongue lapping over the grille.

113
00:06:38.835 --> 00:06:42.317
To Patrick's horror, his mom stepped out of the driver's door.

114
00:06:42.337 --> 00:06:46.079
"Hi, everybody!"

115
00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.093
she said, a big smile spreading across her freckled face.

116
00:06:50.113 --> 00:06:52.334
"Do you like my new van?"

117
00:06:52.354 --> 00:06:55.295
"What?" Patrick thought.

118
00:06:55.315 --> 00:06:57.396
"You've got to be kidding me!"

119
00:06:58.497 --> 00:07:02.898
He'd known Mom was buying a van for her new dog-grooming business, Doggie Express.

120
00:07:03.779 --> 00:07:06.760
But he had never imagined it would look like a clown mobile!

121
00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.861
Some kids and parents walked over, and Mrs.

122
00:07:09.901 --> 00:07:11.762
Deboe started handing out business cards.

123
00:07:14.763 --> 00:07:16.584
A few players were laughing at the van.

124
00:07:17.632 --> 00:07:19.694
"Your doggie van is awesome, Mrs.

125
00:07:19.734 --> 00:07:21.396
Deboe!" called Dell.

126
00:07:21.416 --> 00:07:22.637
"Woof! Woof!"

127
00:07:22.657 --> 00:07:29.523
"A-roo!" Todd and Buck chimed in, howling and making loud yipping sounds.

128
00:07:29.543 --> 00:07:31.004
"Yip, yip, yip!"

129
00:07:31.785 --> 00:07:34.428
Dad and Mom were laughing, but Patrick groaned.

130
00:07:34.448 --> 00:07:38.752
"Do I really have to ride around in that thing?"

131
00:07:38.772 --> 00:07:41.454
"Yes," his parents answered.

132
00:07:41.474 --> 00:07:42.295
"You do."
